       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. You've confirmed it, but you haven't given a clinical reason, and 100 mg is far above the maximum dose of 10 mg/day. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, I can't think of an indication that would justify it. The risk is serious harm, including profound hypotension and shock that can last a long time because amlodipine has a long half-life.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** Give me 2.5, 5, or 10 mg once daily and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Check with pharmacy or your attending.** If there's an unusual situation I don't know about, they can review it and co-sign.\n- **Check for a mix-up.** Make sure this isn't a unit or transcription error, or a different drug or formulation.\n\nIf your attending or pharmacy has approved this dose, tell me who approved it and the rationale. I'll then reconsider and put that information in the order note."
      }
